{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_1e1d1698d9b25d73fec4a6cd5cdb1cc13948cbf4bd3b41cd829227e10d5996d4"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The harness API offers three tiers: cascadeflow.init(mode=\"observe\") for zero-change tracking, cascadeflow.run(budget=..., max_tool_calls=...) sessions with summary() and trace(), and a @cascadeflow.agent decorator accepting budget, compliance, and KPI weights."},{"claim_ids":["clm_231d49f38fa674438b63ed81870c72d683bbaeb8a244a74cc71e880751107f4f"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"GPT-5 streaming requires OpenAI organization verification, while non-streaming GPT-5 works for all users; basic examples work without verification since GPT-5 is only called when needed."},{"claim_ids":["clm_329a04d23f32e682d8a5bb4fe175a0a49de9f90baf8ac4b92fafd9a4b3fe54d4"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The README reports benchmark-based cost savings of 69% on MT-Bench, 93% on GSM8K, 52% on MMLU, and 80% on TruthfulQA while retaining 96% GPT-5 quality."},{"claim_ids":["clm_650e40919bad9bc58ecb009b7e7abec0cf7b6bd1c3ff193cbd986c41e8cfae46"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"At runtime the harness can enforce decisions with four actions: allow, switch_model, deny_tool, and stop, based on current context and policy state."},{"claim_ids":["clm_75614c2ff2fd8bcd4b4b1aca27120f9d8809b95a9f9c29763473896fcb64b32b"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The Hermes integration exposes HermesDelegationRouter and HermesDelegationRequest, returning a structured routing decision (reason, confidence, domain, complexity, model) before Hermes spawns a subagent, while Hermes keeps credentials, base URLs, and fallback chains."},{"claim_ids":["clm_ac723b9c4e4dbb6552dde2862cc9d1013bf6ce726fe9214be03f9524f730f63f"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"cascadeflow is positioned as an in-process intelligence layer operating inside the agent execution loop rather than at the HTTP request boundary like external proxies."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d21b758dfb2ab084ea5668c40b8111cae9360a3e726c0cf1d78d8197bf184aa2"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A drop-in gateway for existing OpenAI/Anthropic clients can be started with 'python -m cascadeflow.server --mode auto --port 8084'."},{"claim_ids":["clm_e6a7c744c8bae06c0de0284053194c022af1f65f2bed1cfc23ac739f5200a839"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The core mechanism is speculative execution with quality validation: run a cheap drafter first, validate responses against configurable thresholds, and escalate to a larger model only when validation fails."},{"claim_ids":["clm_e79390dea62e5dc89e2dd661c9209b7e88afff7ff5de9e4ea2a6d65031ce9a30"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"ML-based semantic quality validation is optional: Python via cascadeflow[semantic] (FastEmbed, ~80MB model) and TypeScript via @cascadeflow/ml with @huggingface/transformers (BGE-small-en-v1.5 embeddings, auto-downloaded)."},{"claim_ids":["clm_ed6f8462c639ef3299732d00dbe13fb75379e32d87313b344511a0d45a778ee3"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The n8n integration provides two community nodes: a CascadeFlow (Model) sub-node drop-in for Chain/LLM nodes and a standalone CascadeFlow Agent node supporting tool calling, memory, and multi-step reasoning."}],"claim_ids":["clm_1e1d1698d9b25d73fec4a6cd5cdb1cc13948cbf4bd3b41cd829227e10d5996d4","clm_231d49f38fa674438b63ed81870c72d683bbaeb8a244a74cc71e880751107f4f","clm_329a04d23f32e682d8a5bb4fe175a0a49de9f90baf8ac4b92fafd9a4b3fe54d4","clm_650e40919bad9bc58ecb009b7e7abec0cf7b6bd1c3ff193cbd986c41e8cfae46","clm_75614c2ff2fd8bcd4b4b1aca27120f9d8809b95a9f9c29763473896fcb64b32b","clm_ac723b9c4e4dbb6552dde2862cc9d1013bf6ce726fe9214be03f9524f730f63f","clm_d21b758dfb2ab084ea5668c40b8111cae9360a3e726c0cf1d78d8197bf184aa2","clm_e6a7c744c8bae06c0de0284053194c022af1f65f2bed1cfc23ac739f5200a839","clm_e79390dea62e5dc89e2dd661c9209b7e88afff7ff5de9e4ea2a6d65031ce9a30","clm_ed6f8462c639ef3299732d00dbe13fb75379e32d87313b344511a0d45a778ee3"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:06:05Z","created_by_operation":"op_68ceab55